-- Two overloads of one mixfix pattern in ONE module, on numbers and on strings,
-- each with a herald of its own. A call reads the herald of the overload it
-- resolved to. The prefix counterpart of this is the second pair of overloads in
-- jl4/examples/ok/pattern-matching-overloads-own-annotations.l4.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the smaller number of %a% and %b%
`the lower of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A STRING
      b IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
@nlg whichever of %a% and %b% comes first in the alphabet
`the lower of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

#EVAL `the lower of` 3 `and` 4
#EVAL `the lower of` "x" `and` "y"

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`own cap` n MEANS `the lower of` n `and` 100

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`own first name` s MEANS `the lower of` s `and` "m"
